{"uid":"124f1d02ccdbdd6c","name":"test_a_primary_owner_who_loses_a_required_scope_is_narrowed_not_locked_out","fullName":"tests.test_projects#test_a_primary_owner_who_loses_a_required_scope_is_narrowed_not_locked_out","historyId":"06f1ce5655b77bc2e8c16003ec88ab9f","time":{"start":1789490017018,"stop":1789490017065,"duration":47},"description":"`is_eligible_for_owner_role` gates *granting* the `owner` role\n    (`P1-C`); this proves the same `{operator, approver}` conjunction is\n    also re-checked on every request against the caller's own *live*\n    scopes. `@lapsing-owner` creates the project with both scopes (the\n    project's real primary owner, via `CaliberProject.owner`, not merely\n    an `owner`-role membership row) -- then loses `approver` at the\n    platform-identity level, same as any other config change an operator\n    might make for an unrelated reason.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>is_eligible_for_owner_role</code> gates <em>granting</em> the <code>owner</code> role<br />\n(<code>P1-C</code>); this proves the same <code>{operator, approver}</code> conjunction is<br />\nalso re-checked on every request against the caller's own <em>live</em><br />\nscopes. <code>@lapsing-owner</code> creates the project with both scopes (the<br />\nproject's real primary owner, via <code>CaliberProject.owner</code>, not merely<br />\nan <code>owner</code>-role membership row) -- then loses <code>approver</code> at the<br />\nplatform-identity level, same as any other config change an operator<br />\nmight make for an unrelated reason.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789489477071,"stop":1789489477071,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factor